00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.160 align:start position:0%
 
back here at the white house the  likelihood of a summit between President  Trump and Kim Jong Hwan seems to be  growing by the day a top North Korean  official has been dispatched to New York  he will meet meet with America's top  diplomat Wednesday all of this comes  less than a week after President Trump  canceled the planned  Singapore summit chief White House  correspondent and John Roberts is here  on the North Lawn with me too not Jim  jump right good evening to you the White  House isn't yet ready to declare the  summit back on and even if it is back on  it may be impossible to hold it on June  the 12th may have to be slid back a  couple of days but the planning is  proceeding full steam ahead President  Trump today maintained his upbeat  assessment of a summit with Kim jong-un  tweeting this morning that one of the  highest ranking officials in North Korea  was headed to the US kim gyeong-cheol  the vice chairman of north korea heading  now to new york the president tweeted  solid response to my letter thank you  kim yeongcheol was the head of north  korea's cyber spying agency and was  sanctioned by the Obama administration  in 2015 for allegedly orchestrating the  hack attack on Sony Pictures he was also  at Kim jong-un side during the meeting  with South Korean president moon jae-in  the turnaround with North Korea happened  after President Trump shocked the world  sending Kim a letter last Thursday  calling off the summit this president in  that letter last week I thought really  got some kinetic energy going folks all  of a sudden said wow this may actually  not happen and if we want it to happen  then we're going to start moving it ever  since then practically North Korea South  Korea and the United States have been  making very positive moves  the administration has two teams in the  region one led by deputy chief of staff  Jo Hagan is in Singapore to work out the  logistics of a possible summit another  team is at the DMZ nailing down some of  the diplomatic issues and Secretary of  State Mike Pompeo will meet in New York  tomorrow with kim yeongcheol we are  still finalizing exactly what these  meetings will look like but the  secretary will be heading up to New York  tomorrow and I believe returning  sometime on Thursday I think it's pretty  impressive thinking about where we were  one year ago where we were even six  months ago for that matter and now we  have three simultaneous meetings taking  place on this  to talk about the denuclearization of  the Korean Peninsula and president Trump  will have one last meeting with Japanese  Prime Minister Shinzo Abe a ahead of  June 12th  obby will visit the White House next  Thursday to talk strategy Japan wants to  make sure its interests are represented  the threat from North Korea's  intermediate-range ballistic missiles  and Japanese citizens kidnapped by North  Korea at their mar-a-lago summit an  April President Trump promised he would  raise it we're going to do everything  possible to have them brought back and  bring them back to Japan I gave you that  promise  president Trump is sought Chinese  President Xi Jinping's help in bringing  North Korea to the table but today a  possible complicating factor the White  House announcing it will soon impose a  25% tariff on 50 billion dollars in  Chinese imports and implement investment  restrictions and enhanced export  controls on us technology China  responded tersely to what it saw as a  negotiating tactic in broader trade  talks in a statement the Ministry of  Commerce saying we are surprised by the  strategic statement released by the  White House but at the same time it is  somewhat expected and President Trump  got some blowback over a tweet he set  out on Memorial Day when he posted happy  Memorial Day those who died for our  great country would be very happy and  proud at how well our country is doing  today best economy in decades lowest  unemployment numbers for blacks and  Hispanics ever and women in 18 years  rebuilding our military and so much more  nice that prompted a sober response from  the former chairman of the Joint Chiefs  of Staff General Martin Dempsey tweeting  this day of all days of the year should  not be about any one of us no matter how  prestigious or powerful no matter how  successful we perceive ourselves to be  the president's tone was far different  when he gave the yearly address at the  Arlington National Cemetery honoring  those who gave their lives in defense of  this country the first daughter Ivanka  Trump seemed to get it just a bad pitch  perfect when she treated it tweeted out  quote as we remember our fallen  servicemen and women our hearts are  filled with gratitude for their  sacrifice and  of their courage breath another aspect  of Ivanka Trump raising some eyebrows  about the business sighs some people are  casting a skeptical eye at the fact that  she recently received from China seven  new trademarks and then shortly after  that the president cut a deal with Xi  Jinping to resurrect the Chinese telecom  giant ZTE Abigail Klem who runs the  Ivanka Trump brand for the first  daughter said that this business as  usual they were simply trying to protect  the trademarks in an era when there are  so many trademark violations the White  House pointing out that while the  President did cut a deal with Xi Jinping  to save ZTE he also this morning said  that he was set to impose a 25% tariff  on 50 billion dollars worth of Chinese  goods thought of moving parts John as  always thank you

